-> game_intro

=== game_intro ===
Alright... that's the last of them. #speaker: Me
Setting down a large cardboard box fit for a giant, I rub my shoulder in small quick motions, releasing the tension from a long hectic day.
New decorations, boxes of supplies, and a whole lot of fresh ingredients. #speaker: Me
All set and ready to go! #speaker: Me
Looking around at my newly decorated space, I feel a sense of pride.
Everything just screams <i>'autumn is here.'</i>
I yawn, blinking the sleep away from my eyes.
One sleep-deprived baker, <i>also</i> ready to go. #speaker: Me
This is definitely the longest I've ever stayed here, <i>especially</i> alone.
I hadn't even realized how quickly it got dark out, or just how abandoned the street was.
Thinking to myself, I recount just how many late nights I've spent carrying shipments in.
That was...let's see... the <i>fourth</i> time this week I've had to restock! #speaker: Me
I swear, sometimes it feels like I'm losing ingredients faster than I bake. #speaker: Me
I chuckle fondly.
Grandma would say it's pixie's playing their tricks, but I say it's just good business.
Fall truly is my busiest season. It's the time of year when the <i>whole</i> world's cozy cravings come out from hiding.
Buttery flaky apple pies, sweet potato donuts, fluffy mushroom bread. It's a never-ending baked goods parade.
The cold weather just seems to bring folks together, and it's my job to make sure they have a piping-hot treat to cure what ails them.
And don't get me started on the aftermath. I think I might still have some pie dough on my head.
Running a hand through my hair, my fingers graze over a tiny clump of flour sticking near the inner roots.
Yup. Still there. #speaker: Me
But, even though I'm up to <i>my hair</i> in work, I wouldn't trade my bakery for anything in the world.
-> DONE

=== moth_r1 ===
Was that the door? I could have sworn I made sure to lock up...
* [Better stay quiet.]
    Nope. Not today.
    I've seen enough slasher movies to know you should <i>never</i> call out to the spooky figure.
    I'm staying right here, quiet as a mouse.
    As I steady my breath, I lean down behind the counter, just out of sight, watching the door closely.
* [Who's there?]
    Um, excuse me? The shop's currently closed right now, please come back tomorrow! #speaker: Me
    Preferably when we're still open...
- What is that? #speaker: Me
Shock reels me back on my feet, causing me to nearly crash into the newly placed stock behind me.
O-O-Ok, that is a <i>very</i> large bug. Or wait... is it an insect? No, a <i>moth</i>!
My eyes desperately scan for answers.
Halloween is tomorrow, right? Yeah! It's got to be some sort of Halloween thing!
Looking into this creature's wide empty eyes, I feel an increasing sense of panic.
T-That looks pretty dang real.
<i>The lights.</i> #speaker: Posh Moth Lady
A scratchy drawled voice fills the space, deep and booming.
Gripping the edge of the counter, I desperately search for something, <i>anything,</i> to wield as a weapon.
Rolling pin, knife, <i>bug spray??</i>
Ah no time, no time, no time!
S-Stay back! #speaker: Me
I brace myself, ready to meet my end, my whole life flashing before my eyes.
The lights are positively scrumptious in here my dear! Yes, very comforting indeed. Where ever did you purchase them? #speaker: Posh Moth Lady
Wait.
What?
I look up to see the lady moth blissfully standing in the shop's interior, huddled beneath the lights I put up earlier.
Oh, those? I mean just online. #speaker: Me
Online? But were they not quite expensive? Shipping is a menace in this country! #speaker: Posh Moth Lady
She flicks her head in confusion.
Does she often shop online?
You would think so, right? But no, they were actually pretty cheap for the whole bundle, so I got a couple of them. #speaker: Me
You know in case the other ones, like stop working or... something. #speaker: Me
I shift awkwardly on my feet, my hands clenched white at the knuckles.
What is even happening right now?
Ah, a truly tasteful measure! #speaker: Posh Moth Lady
You cannot believe how hard it is to find establishments with good lighting these days, let alone open so late! #speaker: Posh Moth Lady
These bitter autumn nights are cold as death, just dreadful for my delicate health! #speaker: Posh Moth Lady
I-I feel faint as a lily. #speaker: Posh Moth Lady
Now that you mention it, she really doesn't look all that great.
I mean, I don't know how she <i>usually</i> looks, but she <i>does</i> look awfully chilly right now.
Right on cue, she begins to cough, her scratchy voice now very apparently the beginnings of a sore throat.
O-Oh, would you please fetch me a little something to warm me up dearie? #speaker: Posh Moth Lady
Staring at her pained expression, I suddenly feel a sense of duty.
When I first opened this shop, I took a vow.
I told myself I'd always do my best to help each and every soul that walked through these doors.
And at the end of the day, she <i>is</i> a customer, just like everyone else!
Well, not <i>exactly</i> like everyone else, but a customer all the same!
Swallowing down any doubts, I slip into a bright shining smile like it's second nature.
Welcome in Miss, please make yourself comfortable! Now, what can I get you? #speaker: Me
Make me something sautéed and hearty, topped with a little something sweet. #speaker: Posh Moth Lady
Oh how I miss France... #speaker: Posh Moth Lady
-> DONE

